\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces DELT-Hit is organized into analysis modules (blue) that align with the wet-lab DEL workflow (green). DEL synthesis (A) proceeds through iterative cycles of building block addition and encoding. Libraries are then screened in affinity-based selection experiments (B), after which retained DNA tags are PCR-amplified and sequenced. DELT-Hit uses Cutadapt\cite  {ref29} to demultiplex sequencing reads (C) with user-defined error tolerances and produces count matrices for combinations of selection and building block codes. In parallel, library compounds can be enumerated in silico (D) from building block structures and reaction SMIRKS definitions, and molecular properties can be calculated (E). DELT-Hit then combines count data and chemical information for hit analysis (F), quality control, enrichment ranking, and interactive data exploration. The workflow also exports molecular representations, including Morgan fingerprints and BERT embeddings, for downstream machine-learning analyses.}}{3}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:figure1}{{1}{3}{DELT-Hit is organized into analysis modules (blue) that align with the wet-lab DEL workflow (green). DEL synthesis (A) proceeds through iterative cycles of building block addition and encoding. Libraries are then screened in affinity-based selection experiments (B), after which retained DNA tags are PCR-amplified and sequenced. DELT-Hit uses Cutadapt\cite {ref29} to demultiplex sequencing reads (C) with user-defined error tolerances and produces count matrices for combinations of selection and building block codes. In parallel, library compounds can be enumerated in silico (D) from building block structures and reaction SMIRKS definitions, and molecular properties can be calculated (E). DELT-Hit then combines count data and chemical information for hit analysis (F), quality control, enrichment ranking, and interactive data exploration. The workflow also exports molecular representations, including Morgan fingerprints and BERT embeddings, for downstream machine-learning analyses}{figure.caption.2}{}}
